{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/813843-caern-of-vengeance-need-help","id":813843,"title":"Caern of Vengeance - need help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-21T19:28:17-08:00","id":813843,"title":"Caern of Vengeance - need help","content":"Would a Caern of Vengeance be a caern of Glory or Honor? And what should its powers be like?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking it should be similar to a caern of Rage, but want to know other opinions.<br /> <br /> I thought Honor might be appropriate because it's similar to justice, but would be reserved for correcting wrongs that go unaddressed by the law, the powerful, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T22:20:18-08:00","id":813919,"title":"","content":"I think it could go either way. In order to have a need for vengeance, some law or trust must have been violated... and now attaining vengeance has become a matter of honor. Alternatively, if the subject of the Caern's vengeance is a mighty opponent, the vengeance in question may be less about a specific slight and more about this particular foe. If this is the case, I could also see glory as a motivator. In additition to Rage, Strength or even Sorrow could be appropriate.<br /> <br /> What is the scenario? Where is the Caern and who are its enemies?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T22:45:47-08:00","id":813927,"title":"","content":"I am basing it on the legend of the <a href=\"http://digital.library.upenn.edu/women/gask/tales/MOUSE.html\" target=\"_blank\">Mouse Tower of Bingen</a>. Short synopsis is that in a time of great famine, people appealed to a greedy bishop to distribute stored grain. Rather than do so, he cruelly lied that he would, trapped them in a storehouse, and then burned them to death. Later, swarms of rats appeared and devoured him alive.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bingen_am_Rhein\" target=\"_blank\">Bingen am Rhein</a> is a real city, and tradition names the bishop as being <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hatto_II\" target=\"_blank\">Hatto II</a>, archbishop of Mainz.<br /> <br /> I thought it would make a great caern for Bone Gnawers. The idea being that the Wyld birthed a swarm of materialized rat spirits to destroy the offender. Later, spirits lead some Bone Gnawers to the place where the barn burned, and they erected a caern. I figure the legend indicates the caern is quite powerful - at least rank 3, maybe 4. Therefore, it serves as a center for a rare Bone Gnawer exclusive caern. It acts as a worldwide center for the Bone Gnawers to unleash retribution on their worst enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T07:47:32-08:00","id":814122,"title":"","content":"Based on the legend being used I would make it honor. I'd also be sorely tempted to have this Caern be in engaged in a war with the Inquisition and the Catholic Church.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T11:14:00-08:00","id":814284,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't be surprised if a few rat kin don't pop up now again","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-22T14:13:07-08:00","id":814448,"title":"","content":"Vengeance is Glory. Justice is Honor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}